        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ray Stark, Stanley Kubrick, Eliot Hyman\n- Companies: Seven Arts Productions\n- Products: The World of Suzie Wong, West Side Story, The Misfits, Lolita, The Night of the Iguana, Reflections in a Golden Eye, Funny Girl, The Goodbye Girl, The Toy, Annie, Steel Magnolias, Operation Bullshine\n- Topics: film production, film release\n\nFacts:\n- In 1957, Ray Stark and Eliot Hyman founded Seven Arts Productions.\n- In 1961, Ray Stark produced The World of Suzie Wong, West Side Story, and The Misfits.\n- In 1962, Ray Stark produced Lolita.\n- In 1962, Lolita was a British-American black comedy-drama film directed by Stanley Kubrick.\n- In 1963, Seven Arts Productions released Operation Bullshine in the United States.\n- In 1964, Ray Stark produced The Night of the Iguana.\n- In 1967, Ray Stark produced Reflections in a Golden Eye.\n- In 1968, Ray Stark produced Funny Girl.\n- In 1977, Ray Stark produced The Goodbye Girl.\n- In 1982, Ray Stark produced The Toy and Annie.\n- In 1989, Ray Stark produced Steel Magnolias.\n- Ray Stark’s background as a literary and theatrical agent helped prepare him to produce dynamic and profitable films from the 1960s through the 1990s.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
